# Environment Variables for Worker Deployment

## Required for Worker (Railway/Render)

```bash
# Redis Connection (for BullMQ Queue)
REDIS_URL=rediss://default:YOUR_PASSWORD@YOUR_HOST:6379

# MongoDB Connection
MONGO_URI=mongodb+srv://username:password@cluster.mongodb.net/database

# Gemini API (for PDF text extraction)
API_KEY_GEMINI=your_gemini_api_key_here

# Upstash Redis REST API (for caching)
UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL=https://your-redis.upstash.io
UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN=your_token_here
```

## Optional (if needed)

```bash
# Node Environment
NODE_ENV=production

# Cloudinary (if worker uploads images)
Cloudname=your_cloud_name
APIkey=your_api_key
APIsecret=your_api_secret
```

---

## How to Get These Values

### REDIS_URL
1. Go to your Upstash dashboard
2. Select your Redis database
3. Copy the **Redis connection string** (starts with `rediss://`)
4. Format: `rediss://default:password@host:port`

### MONGO_URI
1. Go to MongoDB Atlas dashboard
2. Click "Connect" → "Connect your application"
3. Copy the connection string
4. Replace `<password>` with your actual password

### API_KEY_GEMINI
1. Go to https://makersuite.google.com/app/apikey
2. Create a new API key
3. Copy the key

### UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL & TOKEN
1. Go to Upstash dashboard
2. Select your Redis database
3. Scroll to "REST API" section
4. Copy both URL and TOKEN

---

## Deployment Checklist

### Vercel (API Only)
- ✅ Keep all existing environment variables
- ✅ Add: `CLEANUP_SECRET=your-secret-password`

### Railway/Render (Worker Only)
- ✅ REDIS_URL
- ✅ MONGO_URI
- ✅ API_KEY_GEMINI
- ✅ UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL
- ✅ UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN

---

## Security Notes

- ⚠️ Never commit `.env` file to Git
- ⚠️ Use different secrets for production/development
- ⚠️ Rotate secrets regularly
- ⚠️ Limit API key permissions when possible
